# Module map

Follow `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Thin HTTP in `api/`. Business logic in domain packages. Prompts are files under `prompts/`, not hardcoded strings in Python.

| Package | Owns |
|---|---|
| `identity/` | Phone → persona, permissions, unknown sender |
| `conversation/` | State, language, orchestrator, turn, voice |
| `safety/` | Rules + evaluator + escalation — **no LLM calls** |
| `triage/` | Extraction, question batching, MSK, non-MSK, summary |
| `matching/` | Specialty match + ranking |
| `booking/` | Flow, Paystack client, status machine |
| `physio/` | Onboarding, availability, alerts, notes, check-in, payouts |
| `family/` | Access, permissions, relay |
| `partner/` | Referral, fee confirmation, urgent flag |
| `admin/` | Escalation, verification queue, broadcast, stats digest |
| `audit/` | Append-only logger |
| `llm/` | Gemini wrapper, prompt builder, RAG |
| `api/webhooks/` | WhatsApp + Paystack (verify, enqueue) |
| `api/internal/` | Physio profile, admin panel, partner portal, receipts **APIs** |

If a file grows past one job, split it. Do not dump new features into `orchestrator.py`.
